    "q-107159": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107159",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n¬P⇔(P∨Q)\\,≡\\,[¬P⇒(P∨Q)]∧\n$$\n\nWhat expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n¬P⇔(P∨Q)\\,≡\\,[¬P⇒(P∨Q)]∧[\\,(P∨Q)⇒¬P\\,].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $(P∨Q)⇒¬P.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
