    "q-107158": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107158",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$¬A⇔B≡$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬A⇔B≡(¬A⇒B)∧(B⇒¬A)\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n(¬A⇒B)∧(B⇒¬A)≡(¬¬A∨B)∧(¬B∨¬A)\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n(¬¬A∨B)∧(¬B∨¬A)≡(¬¬A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n(¬¬A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)≡(A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
